  function threnody(){
    return `${heading("ENTITY RECORD / 02","The <em>Threnody.</em>","The archive has a name, a shape, and a history of edits. It does not have a reliable account of what the name refers to.","NS-014")}
      <div class="two-col"><div class="prose">
        <div class="threnody-art"><div class="threnody-glyph"><i></i></div><span class="specimen-caption">FIG. 014-A // FORM RECONSTRUCTION, NOT A PORTRAIT</span><span class="specimen-stamp">PARTIAL</span></div>
        <p class="lead">A triangular face appears in several records that should not share a source.</p>
        <p>The term <em>Threnody</em> is attached to an entity described in the surviving material as appointed, rather than born into its role. The appointment is referenced more often than the appointing authority. The archive has not preserved enough context to make that distinction useful.</p>
        <p>Some copies call it a deity. Others use a word that translates poorly and has been omitted from this public record. The triangular mark is the only stable visual detail across the fragments, and even that may be a copying error.</p>
        <div class="note-box"><strong>EDITORIAL WARNING / 014-B</strong>This page is a public extract. It is not a complete account of the Threnody, its purpose, or its place in the wider NullShift canon.</div>
        <h2>What can be said</h2><p>There is a recurring association with a role, a curse, and an authority that does not appear to explain itself. The record does not establish whether these are literal facts, symbolic descriptions, or later interpretations.</p>
